From 1d4fc6e1779bdf190cfd2d158f679f3324070d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:13:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add the six community formats

The Format dropdown now offers the Orre community's settled competitive
formats on every platform, alongside Free and OU: three rulesets times two
entry shapes. Standard (Orre Colosseum / Hoenn Stadium) keeps the canon
rules; Unlimited (Orre / Hoenn) allows every Pokemon and item, Soul Dew
included, with Species and Item Clause still applying; Limited (Orre /
Hoenn) plays at LEVEL 50 with all remaining Gen 1-3 legendaries banned on
top of the Standard list. Orre shapes enter 4 of 6, Hoenn shapes 3 of 6.

The in-game rules pin gained the full matrix: the Lv50 stock tournament
preset (DOL slot 2, verified byte-identical to the Lv100 slot 3 outside its
level words) joins the Lv100 one, and the entries halfword (word 6) is
patched to 4 or 3 per shape. FormatRules validates per format -- the
validators take the format key, Limited adds the legendary list and a
max-level-50 check (Showdown "Level:" lines, bundle mons and save reads all
carry levels; Android's paste-note bridge passes a levels array now) -- and
every refusal, note and hosting error names the actual format. Public-lobby
tags: [Orre] [Orre-U] [Orre-L] [Hoenn] [Hoenn-U] [Hoenn-L] [OU], shared
byte-identically by both platforms.

Also: RegenerateIni's session-boundary removal calls no longer re-emit the
picked format's rules lines (a picked format used to leave its block at
rest in the INI between sessions), and the missing Core/System.h include in
BattleCustomizer is added (the previous patch did not compile alone).
